  "method#48": {
   "stands": "In use: an Opus reviewer found a serious defect in 9 of 14 [M] Opus-built clinic slices. Our tests resolve only ±11 to 14 points [E], wider than the 2 to 8 point [M] tier gap."
  },
  "method#13": {
   "how": "Each PR title starts with its phase id and the body names the branch; a lane board maps phase, session, branch, PR and state."
  },
  "tokens#20": {
   "how": "Pick the model by window size as well as by its token rate; spend Opus at xhigh only where evidence is thin; verify only where it moves a decision."
  },
  "method#47": {
   "stands": "Modelled on guessed inputs: at middle values 25.7 [G] cheap-call equivalents and 21.2 % [G] wrong per piece, against 29.9 [G] and 11.2 % [G] for the strong model alone."
  },
  "owner#0": {
   "name": "One-page view for me beside agent packets"
  },
  "owner#10": {
   "name": "Six interactive demos on my harness v2 page"
  },
  "owner#11": {
   "next": "I answer KS-D1; the free audit runs, then I am asked again before any build. Defaults never cover installs, hooks, permissions, deletes or anything leaving this PC."
  },
